at  ordeal as you all know he doesn't like  giving anything away so that's why i'm  assuming he's still leading up to that  moment i'm very interested in seeing  what happens when brienne gets jaime  back to lady stoneheart now if this is  in fact the case then that most likely  means he still has a lot more writing to  do before he gets the wins of winter  finished then again i am only guessing  the fact of the matter is no one knows  exactly how much he has done except for  him unfortunately the only thing we all  know for sure is that it's still not  here let me know what all of you think  about these new updates now i know some  of you think we will never see the winds  of winter but i'm on the other side of  that fence at least for now like i have  said before i go back and forth on this  myself some days i think it will be here  soon then on other days i think we will  never see it at all  thankfully we have house of the dragon  for now that's where my main focus will  be for the foreseeable future now that  we're only about 3 months away from the  first episode you will be seeing a hell  of a lot more videos from me if you have  any video ideas regarding house of the  dragon leave them down below i'm always  open for suggestions  also don't forget to subscribe if you  want to be entered into the giveaway for  the copy of fire and blood the winner of  that giveaway will be announced on july  1st  this is a book of imaginary history  chronicling the targaryen kings of  westeros it provides a context and a  background for everything that happens  in a in a song of ice and fire and it's  uh not actually written by me it's  written by archmaester gildane of the  citadel of old town who's a a very  distinguished scholar but also a  somewhat idiosyncratic and crotchety old  man who has strong opinions on the  historical figures he's writing about so  uh some of his uh views may creep into  the text i don't  vouch for its authenticity  the targaryens were people  the